{
  "_comment": "SHARED SETTINGS DEFINITION — the scene half of the settings pair (with scripts/shared/settings.lua). Carries the settings screen data model (video/audio/input rows) + chrome, authored ONCE here instead of copied into every scene file (Aaron 2026-08-14). UnifiedSettingsScene resolves settings.* against this block; main_scene_styles() merges it back onto the shell carrier until settings is a fully self-contained scene. INTERIM: the tree is still built by settings.lua M.tree() (the static-tree + derive conversion is the rest of content-layer item #8); dead pre-walker residue (nav_items, titlebar hint/close, cycler/segment, min_margin) is pruned + the window/control skins promote to Rust defaults in Stage 3.",
  "styles": {
    "settings": {
      "window": {
        "w": 1180,
        "h": 726,
        "min_margin": 32,
        "radius": 4,
        "fill_top": "$stone3",
        "fill_bot": "$stone1",
        "border": "$edge2",
        "shadow": "$shadow",
        "shadow_dy": 18,
        "shadow_feather": 46,
        "shadow_grow": 4
      },
      "titlebar": {
        "h": 52,
        "pad_x": 30,
        "wash": "$accent_wash",
        "seam": "$seam",
        "_fill_note": "fill_top/fill_bot = the declared `wash` so draw_panel_bg actually tints the bar (was falling back to the dark PANEL constant); `color` = `title_color` so the title text picks it up (draw_text reads `color`/`label_color`, not `title_color`).",
        "fill_top": "$accent_wash",
        "fill_bot": "$accent_wash",
        "color": "$ink_bright",
        "mark": "$bronze",
        "title": "$set_settings",
        "title_size": 21,
